 ## 3. Sharing
 
-A zone share carries an NXDN channel's tag as it is ([zone-share.md](zone-share.md) 4.2): the block is 3 octets, inside
-the share's limit of 64.
+A zone share carries an NXDN channel's tag as it is ([zone-share.md](zone-share.md) 4.2). The key itself stays in the
+radio's keyring. Provision the same key on the receiving radio before transmitting.
+
+## 4. 15-bit voice scrambler (kind 8)
+
+Kind 8 uses the same rate, squelch and RAN bytes (0–2) as kind 4. Byte 3 is 0x02 and byte 4 is the key ID 0–63.
+This is conventional voice only. An absent or malformed block, a Type-C flag, or a missing key blocks transmission.
+Kind 4's AES-256 and Type-C fields retain their existing meanings. The kind 8 tag uses a DMR receive-only base record.
+Firmware without `CONFIG_NXDN_SCRAMBLER` parks kind 8 and refuses PTT. Readers without tag support see receive-only DMR.
+
+The keyring's traffic record uses system 0xFF, algorithm 1, a key ID 0–63 and a two-byte little-endian seed 1–32767.
+IDs are unique within the algorithm. Conventional RX chooses the key announced in the call; TX uses the channel's
+selected key. Clear conventional voice and AES-256 retain their own receive paths. See [nxdn.md](nxdn.md) for the call
+protocol.
